Modifications: rewritten rather than copied, with a descriptive name in place
of the upstream one, our section order, no em-dashes and no references to
sibling skills. Kept rules: a read-only audit with a second search method
before any edit; occurrences classified as copy, paraphrase, partial, stale or
contradictory; a canonical home chosen with a justification; a location, kind
and action table; explicit approval before mutation; an empty result is valid;
contradictions are never decided silently; unique details are folded into the
home before a copy is cut; no consolidation across a trust boundary without
confirmation; edit per occurrence and report a MISS when a target is absent;
code moves use language-aware tools. Dropped the upstream Python
unicode-safety advice and the paragraph on folding audit artifacts. Added
"Not for" lines naming docs-audit and agent-instructions.
